{"repositoryId":622511745,"availability":"available","full":"TopGunBuild/topgun","name":"topgun","description":"Offline-first in-memory data grid with CRDT sync and a Rust server","category":"Developer tools","language":"Rust","stars":36,"forks":2,"created":"2023-04-02T10:40:52Z","updated":"2026-10-12T22:58:47Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://topgun.build","topics":["crdt","data-grid","database","indexeddb","local-first","offline-first","postgresql","react","realtime","rust","sync","typescript","websocket"],"demo":"https://demo.topgun.build/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-13T06:39:55.171Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-13T06:39:55.171Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-13T06:39:55.171Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-13T06:39:55.171Z","stars":36,"forks":2}],"technologies":["React","Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["[](LICENSE) [](.github/workflows/rust.yml) []( []( []( [](","Build real-time apps that work offline. Local writes are instant and survive disconnects; reconnecting clients sync seamlessly with automatic conflict resolution. Self-host today with the embedded backend, or wire up Postgres when you need it. Apache-2.0, Rust server, TypeScript client. AI agents talk to your data natively through MCP.","TopGun v2 is a complete rewrite. It's not a port — it's a new architecture built to earn production trust; the status note above says what we do and don't yet claim."],"features":["Local-first: Data lives in memory. Reads and writes never wait for network.","Offline support: Changes persist to IndexedDB and sync when reconnected.","Conflict-free merges: Automatic conflict resolution via LWW-Map and OR-Map, with causality tracked by logical clocks.","Efficient delta sync: Only changed data moves over the wire, via Merkle tree comparison.","Pluggable storage: Embedded redb by default; Postgres optional for production; bring your own adapter."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/TopGunBuild/topgun/bl